# Integration mapping for Darling (macOS compatibility)
# Format: upstream_path:goliath_path:action
# Actions: copy, copy+modify, exclude, manual

# This file tracks how upstream Darling code maps to Goliath's integration.
# When the upstream sync workflow runs, it uses this file to understand
# which files to update and which have been customized.

## Core files (direct copy from upstream)
# src/frameworks/:libs/darling_framework/frameworks/:copy
# src/kernel/:libs/darling_framework/kernel/:copy

## Modified files (copied but with Goliath-specific changes)
# Document any modifications here

## Excluded files (not needed for Goliath integration)
# build/:exclude
# tests/:exclude
# docs/:exclude

## Manual integration files (managed by Goliath, not synced)
# Makefile.in:manual
# README.md:manual

## Notes
# - Darling is a large project, we may only integrate specific components
# - Focus on the Darwin syscall translation layer and Mach-O loader
# - Full Darling includes kernel emulation which may not be needed
